const SIT=[["Orders arrive in many places","That is an integration problem before it is a software problem. We connect the channels (website, WhatsApp, email, forms) so each order or enquiry is recorded once and routed automatically, with a person alerted when something needs judgement.",["auto","commerce"]],["Stock and deliveries go wrong","Stock counted in two places and deliveries chased by phone are symptoms of one gap: no single record. We build the order, stock and delivery tracking that gives you one.",["commerce","auto"]],["I have an idea for an app","Ideas are cheapest to fix on paper. We help define who will use the system, what the first useful version does and what it should cost to run, then build that version.",["software","cons"]],["Our software keeps breaking","Software that breaks whenever it is touched usually lacks tests, documentation or both. We assess it, stabilise it and put it on a maintenance footing.",["maint","cons"]],["Our servers or network feel fragile","A single server, shared passwords and no backups are common and fixable. We map what runs where, then harden, back up and monitor it.",["cloud","sec"]],["We want AI to take on repetitive work","AI works best on narrow, checkable jobs: sorting enquiries, drafting replies, extracting data. We build it with limits and a review step, so a person stays in control.",["ai","auto"]],["Legal paperwork is burying us","Bundling, signing and deadline tracking are repeatable workflows, which makes them good candidates for software.",["legal","auto"]],["I am not sure what I need","A normal place to start. A short conversation and a read of what you have is enough to say what kind of help, if any, makes sense.",["cons","maint"]]];
const sitD=i=>{const x=SIT[i];return `<div class="panel"><div class="kick">If this sounds like you</div><h3 style="font-size:28px">${x[0]}</h3><p style="font-size:17px;line-height:1.65;color:var(--mu);margin-top:8px">${x[1]}</p><div class="kick" style="margin-top:22px">Start here</div><div class="bar">${svl(x[2])}</div><div style="margin-top:22px"><button class="btn o" data-go="contact">Talk it through</button></div></div>`};
const TK=[["01","Order tracking","Every order gets one number, wherever it came from.","A website checkout, a WhatsApp message and a walk-in sale land in the same order list with the same statuses: new, paid, picking, packed, out for delivery, delivered. The owner sees what is waiting. The packer sees what to pick. Nobody has to ask whether that one went out.",["One order list fed by the website, social channels and the shop counter","A status workflow with a timestamp and a name on every change","Staff roles, so packers pack and only managers refund","Order history and lookup by customer, phone number or order number"],["Operations software open beside the shelves.","wh"]],["02","Stock tracking","Counts that match the shelf.","When an order is paid, the items are reserved so the last unit is not sold twice. When it ships, the count drops. When something runs low, a reorder list builds itself. A barcode scan at receiving and packing keeps the numbers honest, and a stock-take becomes a check rather than a rebuild.",["Live stock by product, variant and location","Reservations that prevent overselling","Low-stock alerts and reorder lists","Barcode scanning for receiving, picking and stock-takes","Sync between web, social and point of sale"],["Dashboards beside warehouse shelving.","hat"]],["03","Delivery tracking","Know where every parcel is, and tell the customer before they ask.","An order is assigned to a courier or rider with the address, the phone number and the amount to collect. Updates come back from the courier system or the rider's phone: picked up, on the way, delivered, failed. The customer gets a tracking link. Cash collected on delivery is recorded and settled at the end of the day.",["Courier and rider integrations, with delivery zones and fees","Tracking links and SMS or WhatsApp updates","Proof of delivery by photo, signature or one-time code","Cash-on-delivery recording and settlement","Failed-delivery and returns handling"],["A customer tracking a parcel on her phone.","parcel"]],["04","Money tracking","Every payment matched to its order.","Card, bank, wallet and cash payments are recorded against the order they belong to. Failed and duplicate payments are flagged. Refunds are tracked. At the end of the day the owner sees takings by channel, and the accountant receives an export instead of a shoebox of receipts.",["Card, bank and wallet payments through your provider's gateway, confirmed by its callback","Reconciliation of takings by channel and by day","Refunds and partial payments, recorded properly","Margin reporting and export to accounting tools"],["A payment summary on a mobile checkout screen.","chk","50% 80%","220%"]]];
