P.process=function(){return `<section class="sec"><div class="kick">Process</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(34px,4.6vw,56px);max-width:860px">What working with us is actually like.</h1><p class="lead2">Five stages, each ending with something concrete that you approve before the next begins. Select a stage to see what happens in it.</p><div class="two" style="margin-top:28px">${list("pl",PRD.map(p=>p.n),pr)}<div id="det">${PDET(pr)}</div></div></section><section class="sec" style="background:var(--ib);max-width:none"><div style="max-width:1200px;margin:0 auto"><div class="g3"><div class="box"><h3>How we communicate</h3><p>You have one named contact. Progress is reported in writing at an agreed interval, every release is demonstrated, and decisions are recorded so nobody has to remember what was agreed.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>Milestones</h3><p>Each stage ends with a review. Work does not start on the next stage until you have accepted the last one, so you can stop, pause or change direction at a known point.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>When requirements change</h3><p>They usually do. A change is described, we explain what it does to scope, effort and order of work, and you decide: include it now, schedule it later or drop it.</p></div></div><p style="margin-top:28px"><button class="btn o" data-go="contact">Start a conversation</button></p></div></section>`};
