/* work */
P.work=function(){LBR=[];return `<section class="sec"><div class="kick">Work</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(34px,4.6vw,56px);max-width:860px">How we approach building a system.</h1><p class="lead2">Verified client case studies will be published here once we have permission and results we can stand behind. Until then, this is an engineering walk-through of the kind of system we build. It is illustrative and is not a client project.</p>
<div class="panel sc" style="margin-top:28px"><div class="kick">Illustrative walk-through</div><h2>A commerce platform for a small retailer</h2><p class="lead">The brief: one system for a shop that sells on a website, social media and a counter, with stock, payments and delivery tracked together.</p><div class="row">${th(["Commerce platform","","Operations software in use in a packing area. Illustrative.","wh"])}<span style="color:var(--mu);font-size:14px">Illustrative image.</span></div><h3>The problem</h3><p>Orders arrive through three channels. Stock is counted separately on each. Payments are matched by hand and delivery status lives in phone calls.</p><h3>Architecture</h3>${dg([["Channels","Storefront, WhatsApp and counter sales feed one API."],["Order service","The single source of truth for orders and statuses."],["Database","Orders, customers, stock and an audit history."],["Payments","Cards, bank transfers and wallets, confirmed by provider callbacks."],["Delivery","Courier and rider integrations with tracking."],["Operations","Admin dashboard, reporting and monitoring."]])}<h3>Key decisions</h3>${ul(["One order service for every channel, so a rule is written once","Payments confirmed by the provider's callback, never by the customer's browser","Stock reserved when payment succeeds and reduced when the parcel is dispatched","Every status change recorded with who made it and when","Background jobs and retries for anything that depends on a third party"])}<h3>Typical technology</h3><p>Django and PostgreSQL for the core, Next.js for the storefront, payment and courier APIs, AWS for hosting and monitoring.</p><h3>What a verified case study will add</h3><p>The client's context, real screenshots, measured outcomes and what we would do differently.</p><div class="cb"><div><b>Have a similar problem?</b><p>We will tell you what we would build and why.</p></div><button class="btn o" data-go="contact" data-pre="commerce">Discuss a project</button></div></div></section>`};
/* about */
P.about=function(){LBR=[];return `<section class="sec"><div class="kick">About</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(34px,4.6vw,56px);max-width:860px">An engineering company that starts with your operations.</h1><div class="row" style="align-items:flex-start;margin-top:22px"><div style="max-width:660px"><p class="lead2" style="margin-top:0">MeriCloud is a remote-first software and systems engineering company. We build applications, integrations, automation and infrastructure, and we keep them running.</p><p class="lead2">We think a system is only as good as the fit between the software and the people who use it. So the first job is understanding the business, and the second is engineering it properly.</p></div>${th(["About","","Engineers working through a design together.","team"])}</div>
<div class="g3" style="margin-top:36px"><div class="box"><h3>The business side</h3><p>Operations, customers, workflows and the commercial reason for the project. We ask who does the work, what goes wrong and what a good result is worth.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>The technical side</h3><p>Software, integration, automation, hosting, networks and security. We choose technology for the problem, explain the trade-offs and document what we build.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>Where they meet</h3><p>Decisions that look technical, such as which database or which provider, often turn on a business fact. We keep both in the room.</p></div></div>
<h2 style="margin:44px 0 0;font-size:32px">How we work</h2><div class="g4"><div class="box"><h3>Fix before replace</h3><p>We improve what works before proposing a rewrite.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>Small releases</h3><p>Working pieces you can try beat a big reveal after months of silence.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>Design for failure</h3><p>Backups, alerts and recovery are part of the first release.</p></div><div class="box"><h3>Leave it readable</h3><p>Clear code and documentation, so nobody is locked in to us.</p></div></div>
<h2 style="margin:44px 0 0;font-size:32px">What we will not claim</h2><p class="lead2">We do not publish clients, testimonials, certifications or statistics until we can show them. When evidence is missing from this site it is because it is not yet ours to show.</p><p style="margin-top:22px"><button class="btn o" data-go="contact">Talk to our team</button></p></section>`};
/* insights */
const ART=[["Build, buy or connect: how to decide","Technology decisions",["Most businesses facing a software decision have three options, and the right one is rarely the one the first quote assumes.","Buy when the need is common. Accounting, email and basic payroll are solved problems, and custom software for them costs more without doing the job better.","Connect when the tools already exist but do not talk to each other. If staff copy data from one screen to another, the missing piece is usually a link, not a new system. An integration or an automation costs a fraction of a platform.","Build when the way you operate is your advantage: a delivery model, a pricing method or a case-handling process that competitors do not share. That deserves software that fits it exactly.","Three questions help. Is this process the same as everyone else's? What does the manual workaround cost each week? What happens if the vendor changes its pricing or its product?","If the answers are unclear, a short technical assessment is cheaper than choosing wrongly."],["cons","auto","software"]],["What an order tracking system actually tracks","E-commerce",["An order looks like one event. It is a chain: placed, paid, reserved from stock, picked, packed, handed to a courier, delivered, sometimes returned or refunded.","A tracking system records each link, who made it and when. That record answers the questions that otherwise cost an hour each: where is this order, who packed it, why is the stock count wrong, was it paid?","Four things need to be tracked together. Orders, with a status that only moves forward through a defined path. Stock, reserved at payment and reduced at dispatch. Deliveries, with updates from the courier or rider. Money, matched to the order it belongs to.","Tracked separately, they drift apart. Tracked in one system, they cannot disagree.","The practical test is simple: pick any order from last week and ask how long it takes to find its whole story."],["commerce","auto"]],["What to prepare before you contact a software company","Working with us",["You do not need a specification. You need a clear enough picture of the problem for a conversation to be useful.","Write down what is slow, broken or missing, in the words your team would use. Note who does the work today and how long it takes. List the tools involved, including spreadsheets and chat groups.","Gather examples: a typical order, a form, a screenshot of the screen that frustrates people. One real example is worth a page of description.","Decide what a good outcome looks like. Fewer errors, faster replies, one view of the stock: any of these is enough.","Be ready to talk about constraints: a deadline, a budget range, systems that cannot change, people who must approve.","If you cannot answer some of these, say so. Working it out together is part of the first conversation."],["cons","maint"]]];
const artD=i=>{const a=ART[i];return `<div class="panel sc"><div class="kick">${a[1]}</div><h2>${a[0]}</h2>${a[2].map(p=>`<p style="margin:12px 0;font-size:17px">${p}</p>`).join("")}<h3>Related</h3><div class="bar">${svl(a[3])}</div><div class="cb"><div><b>Want to talk it through?</b><p>We are happy to look at your situation.</p></div><button class="btn o" data-go="contact">Discuss a project</button></div></div>`};
P.insights=function(){return `<section class="sec"><div class="kick">Insights</div><h1 style="font-size:clamp(34px,4.6vw,56px);max-width:820px">Practical notes on technology decisions.</h1><p class="lead2">Written to help you decide, whether or not you hire us.</p><div class="two" style="margin-top:28px">${list("arl",ART.map(a=>a[0]),arI)}<div id="det4">${artD(arI)}</div></div></section>`};
